A post effect written as one fragment shader, the simplest kind there is. Each [`VolumeParameter<T>`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.Rendering.VolumeParameter) field reaches the shader as a uniform named after it with an underscore, Amount as _Amount: floats, ints and enums as themselves, bools as a float 0 or 1, colours and Float2 to Float4 as vectors, Texture2D as a sampler2D. The shader reads the colour with Graphite_SampleSource(vUV) and writes outColor.

```csharp
[VolumeComponentMenu("Custom/Invert")]
public sealed class Invert : PostEffect
{
    public VolumeParameter<float> Amount = new(0f);
    public override bool IsActive => Amount.Value > 0f;
    protected override string Shader => """
        uniform float _Amount;
        void main()
        {
            vec4 c = Graphite_SampleSource(vUV);
            outColor = vec4(mix(c.rgb, 1.0 - c.rgb, _Amount), c.a);
        }
        """;
}
```

Effects needing several passes or textures of their own derive from [`VolumeComponent<TFeature>`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.Rendering.VolumeComponent) instead.
